      "title": "[Trip Reports] Replay along Shoshone Lake",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=backcountrypost.com&amp;sz=128\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<div class=\"bbWrapper\">A month and a half ago, or so, I did this hike with Mary and Alex.  It was on Kevin's permit, but he had a family emergency and couldn't do the hike. Kevin came back about a week ago, and after a hike up the Lamar River a little ways (there's a trip report about it), we found we could get reservations for the same trip.  We started at Delacy Creek Trailhead, in the upper right corner, went down along the west side of Shoshone Lake, then up to Lone Star Trailhead.  It was a little over 20...<br/>\n<br/>\n<a class=\"link link--internal\" href=\"https://backcountrypost.com/threads/replay-along-shoshone-lake.12733/\">Read more</a></div>",
